ntfy-desktop is a client for ntfy on the Linux desktop.

It subscribes to a topic and shows what arrives as native notifications. When a message asks
for a decision, it opens a desktop dialog with the options that message carries and sends the
answer back. It also publishes messages, and keeps a local history so nothing is lost while you
are away from the machine.

It does not link Qt or GTK: dialogs are delegated to the desktop's own tool — kdialog on
Plasma, zenity on GNOME — chosen at startup. One build, no cgo, a single binary.

KDE Plasma is the supported target today. GNOME is scaffolded and not yet verified.
